[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065032091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108462#issuecomment-3065032091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108462","id":3065032091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62sK2b","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T10:19:27Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T10:44:19Z","body":"> In _GodotPhysics3D_, the sleeping `RigidBody3D` will wake when another moving `RigidBody3D` is nearby (I'm assuming, I don't know if it's distance based), and thus the first contact will be reported.\n\nWhat's happening in Godot Physics is that because you're using the \"wrong\" node type for the `Ground` node (a `RigidBody3D` instead of a `StaticBody3D`) the ground becomes part of what physics engines refer to as an \"island\", together with `Cube` and `Pusher`, and from what I understand most physics engines wake bodies up per-island rather than per-body, meaning as you move `Pusher` the entire island (including `Cube`) wakes up.\n\nThis would technically happen when using Jolt Physics as well, but frankly the distances between the bodies are big enough that I wouldn't really expect the island grouping to happen at all, so I have to assume this is just because of some difference in how/when the two engines create their islands.\n\nEither way, if you switch `Ground` to be a `StaticBody3D` instead you'll find that at least the waking up behaves the same with both engines.\n\nAs for the contact not being reported properly when using Jolt Physics, that does indeed seem to be a bug of some sort.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065032091/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3065117788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108462#issuecomment-3065117788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108462","id":3065117788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62sfxc","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T11:43:07Z","u